1
00:00:12,479 --> 00:00:17,550
They are here!

2
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:26,693
<i>Maybe you're asking while you're seeing
what I'm seeing right now.</i>

3
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:32,234
<i>Maybe you're asking yourself,
"how many times have I watched this?</i>

4
00:00:32,234 --> 00:00:35,805
<i>Is there anything new?
Is there any new story?"</i>

5
00:00:35,805 --> 00:00:39,007
We love you, Ferell brothers.

6
00:00:48,301 --> 00:00:51,500
<i>Is this all I will see?</i>

7
00:00:51,501 --> 00:00:56,572
<i>Well, don't worry,
because this is not my story.</i>

8
00:01:27,571 --> 00:01:31,340
<i>Oh my, the sun is already high.</i>

9
00:01:41,068 --> 00:01:43,120
Mother?

10
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,319
Father?

11
00:01:44,319 --> 00:01:47,444
- Oh, my child.
- Why didn't you wake me up?

12
00:01:47,444 --> 00:01:49,693
My child, you were sleeping soundly.

13
00:01:49,693 --> 00:01:52,562
We didn't wake you up so you can rest well.

14
00:01:52,562 --> 00:01:54,898
Here, taste this.

15
00:01:54,898 --> 00:01:56,767
Tell me if it's delicious already.

16
00:01:56,767 --> 00:01:58,901
Okay, Mother.

17
00:02:02,906 --> 00:02:04,505
- Is it delicious?
- It's good, Mother,

18
00:02:04,505 --> 00:02:05,976
but there's something missing.

19
00:02:05,976 --> 00:02:07,577
- Does it still lack something?
- It needs a little adjusting.

20
00:02:07,577 --> 00:02:08,870
Oh, okay. I'll leave it up to you.

21
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:10,664
- Yes, Mother.
- Okay, you can take charge.

22
00:02:10,664 --> 00:02:12,805
She's becoming an expert now.

23
00:02:33,003 --> 00:02:35,138
Did you sleep well last night, my child?

24
00:02:35,138 --> 00:02:36,139
Was it okay?

25
00:02:36,139 --> 00:02:37,791
When we checked on you

26
00:02:37,791 --> 00:02:41,061
it seems you were having a nightmare.

27
00:02:41,061 --> 00:02:42,730
Not really, Father.

28
00:02:42,730 --> 00:02:44,064
You're something else.

29
00:02:44,064 --> 00:02:47,134
I dreamt about the book I was reading.

30
00:02:47,134 --> 00:02:48,168
About what?

31
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:49,436
It's about boys, right?

32
00:02:49,436 --> 00:02:51,138
Of course not, Father.

33
00:02:51,138 --> 00:02:52,639
Here you are, denying to death,

34
00:02:52,639 --> 00:02:56,010
even when we saw you talking in your sleep.

35
00:02:56,010 --> 00:03:00,247
You said, "Dave, I love you, Dave.

36
00:03:00,247 --> 00:03:02,916
Don't leave me, Dave..."

37
00:03:02,916 --> 00:03:05,519
Hey Federico, stop teasing your daughter.

38
00:03:05,519 --> 00:03:09,235
She might get mad and end up crying again.

39
00:03:09,235 --> 00:03:12,259
Mother, I'm no longer a crybaby.

40
00:03:12,259 --> 00:03:14,028
I'm a grown woman.

41
00:03:14,028 --> 00:03:18,265
I also have dreams
and a heart that is ready to love.

42
00:03:18,265 --> 00:03:19,696
Wow.

43
00:03:19,696 --> 00:03:24,079
Hey Florencia, stop it.

44
00:03:24,079 --> 00:03:25,939
What do you mean by "grown woman"?

45
00:03:25,939 --> 00:03:28,375
Do you want me to pinch your groin?

46
00:03:28,375 --> 00:03:32,561
And what's this "heart that is ready to love"
are you talking about?

47
00:03:32,561 --> 00:03:35,093
Hey, you, once I find out
that you're flirting around,

48
00:03:35,093 --> 00:03:36,717
I will shave your head.

49
00:03:36,717 --> 00:03:38,385
Lydia, just relax.

50
00:03:38,385 --> 00:03:40,501
What she's saying is right.

51
00:03:40,501 --> 00:03:42,662
She's a grown woman already,
she's no longer a kid.

52
00:03:42,662 --> 00:03:46,226
The earlier we accept it, the better.

53
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:50,731
But, Florence, once you flirt around,

54
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:52,332
you should promise me,

55
00:03:52,332 --> 00:03:57,037
you'll introduce that guy to us
if you decide to flirt around.

56
00:03:57,037 --> 00:04:01,140
Then let's see if he deserves
to be flirted with.

57
00:04:01,842 --> 00:04:04,266
There you go...
You're tolerating your daughter,

58
00:04:04,266 --> 00:04:07,247
that's why your heart is reacting that way.

59
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:08,348
Just take it easy.

60
00:04:08,348 --> 00:04:10,250
Because, Mother and Father,

61
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:13,554
why would I flirt around
if I still have a lot of dreams

62
00:04:13,554 --> 00:04:14,788
I want to achieve?

63
00:04:14,788 --> 00:04:19,793
I want to finish college
so I can get a decent job.

64
00:04:19,793 --> 00:04:21,528
And once I have a good salary,

65
00:04:21,528 --> 00:04:24,531
I'll ask you to stop selling cooked food.

66
00:04:24,531 --> 00:04:28,302
That way, you don't have to wake up early
to go to the market

67
00:04:28,302 --> 00:04:33,340
and you won't get tired cutting
and saute-ing onions.

68
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:35,642
And then we'll relax,

69
00:04:35,642 --> 00:04:39,813
and then we'll watch movies,
right, Father and Mother?

70
00:04:39,813 --> 00:04:45,385
And one more thing,
we will go swimming in Boracay Island,

71
00:04:45,385 --> 00:04:51,792
or we'll stroll around Spain
por ejemplo saying good evening,

72
00:04:51,792 --> 00:04:58,784
good day, or eating delicious food in Italy.

73
00:04:58,784 --> 00:05:02,936
Good evening, it's delicious!

74
00:05:02,936 --> 00:05:04,104
Right, Mother?

75
00:05:04,104 --> 00:05:09,610
Or we can have our pictures taken
in Eiffel Tower in Paris, bonjour!

76
00:05:09,610 --> 00:05:11,411
Enchante!

77
00:05:11,411 --> 00:05:12,746
That's our plan, Mother.

78
00:05:12,746 --> 00:05:16,149
That's never-ending drowning with happiness.

79
00:05:21,522 --> 00:05:23,590
Mother?

80
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:25,292
Did I say something you don't like?

81
00:05:25,292 --> 00:05:26,760
Don't you want to go to Europe?

82
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:30,664
- Would you rather go to America?
- No...

83
00:05:30,664 --> 00:05:31,832
No, my child.

84
00:05:31,832 --> 00:05:33,433
That's okay.

85
00:05:33,433 --> 00:05:36,236
Everything's okay.

86
00:05:36,236 --> 00:05:38,238
I don't know what I did,

87
00:05:38,238 --> 00:05:42,442
because I was blessed by God
with a good daughter.

88
00:05:42,442 --> 00:05:44,969
Thank you.

89
00:05:44,969 --> 00:05:47,304
Mother, you're something else.

90
00:05:48,448 --> 00:05:50,384
Federico, why don't you join us?

91
00:05:50,384 --> 00:05:51,718
It's okay, you can go ahead.

92
00:05:51,718 --> 00:05:54,153
- Federico?
- Here you go.

93
00:05:57,691 --> 00:06:03,029
Florence Dela Cruz, there's a letter for you.

94
00:06:03,930 --> 00:06:06,333
Mother, there's a letter.

95
00:06:06,333 --> 00:06:08,335
- Is that for her?
- What's that letter?

96
00:06:08,335 --> 00:06:09,369
That's the...

97
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:11,738
- That's today?
- That's for today.

98
00:06:13,774 --> 00:06:17,010
Florence Dela Cruz?

99
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:19,946
Mister, there's a letter for me?

100
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:22,546
Do you want me to repeat it?

101
00:06:22,546 --> 00:06:24,259
One more time.

102
00:06:33,293 --> 00:06:37,890
Florence Dela Cruz, here's a letter for you.

103
00:06:38,932 --> 00:06:40,767
Come on, Mother, Father.

104
00:06:40,767 --> 00:06:42,502
- One more time.
- Where are we going?

105
00:06:42,502 --> 00:06:44,605
- Where?
- Where are we going?

106
00:06:44,605 --> 00:06:45,893
- What's happening?
- Here?

107
00:06:45,893 --> 00:06:48,041
Here and then we'll go back again?

108
00:06:48,041 --> 00:06:51,376
- Let's go, Father.
- What's going on, Florence?

109
00:06:51,376 --> 00:06:52,613
- I'm getting confused now.
- Mister...

110
00:06:52,613 --> 00:06:55,415
Is there a letter for me?

111
00:06:55,415 --> 00:06:56,683
I'll do it again.

112
00:06:56,683 --> 00:06:59,720
No need, Mister. That's enough.

113
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:02,188
- Here you go.
- There's a letter...

114
00:07:03,924 --> 00:07:05,659
The letter...

115
00:07:05,659 --> 00:07:06,911
My child, Florence.

116
00:07:06,911 --> 00:07:09,596
Is that the result
of your college admission test?

117
00:07:09,596 --> 00:07:10,592
Is that it?

118
00:07:10,592 --> 00:07:14,755
Yes, Mother,
it's a letter from Gyronella University?

119
00:07:15,638 --> 00:07:17,904
Florence, do you need a chair?

120
00:07:17,904 --> 00:07:19,906
Why don't you sit down first?
You might get dizzy.

121
00:07:19,906 --> 00:07:22,376
Yes, have a seat first.

122
00:07:22,376 --> 00:07:23,443
Don't open it yet.

123
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:26,813
- Sit down first.
- That was fast.

124
00:07:26,813 --> 00:07:32,853
My child, always remember,
whatever happens, it's okay.

125
00:07:32,853 --> 00:07:34,354
It's really okay.

126
00:07:34,354 --> 00:07:37,036
Don't be nervous, Florence. It's okay.

127
00:07:37,036 --> 00:07:39,726
You're overreacting, Mother.

128
00:07:39,726 --> 00:07:40,927
I'm sorry, my child.

129
00:07:40,927 --> 00:07:43,262
That's okay.

130
00:08:13,989 --> 00:08:16,192
I'll talk to her.

131
00:08:20,207 --> 00:08:25,605
Florence, there are other opportunities.

132
00:08:25,605 --> 00:08:30,962
Maybe it's okay if our choice
is just the second or third university.

133
00:08:30,962 --> 00:08:33,876
That's okay, right?

134
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:41,764
Well, Mother, Father...

135
00:08:43,357 --> 00:08:46,626
- I got accepted!
- What? You got accepted!

136
00:08:48,195 --> 00:08:51,598
My daughter got accepted!

137
00:08:51,598 --> 00:08:53,300
She got accepted!

138
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:57,593
Neighbors, Florence got accepted into the GU!

139
00:08:58,605 --> 00:09:00,240
Congratulations!

140
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:04,443
Yes!

141
00:09:58,131 --> 00:09:59,132
There you go...

142
00:09:59,132 --> 00:10:00,367
Still nothing?

143
00:10:00,367 --> 00:10:02,469
- Nothing?
- Go ahead and sit down.

144
00:10:02,469 --> 00:10:07,040
- I'll take care of it.
- Don't worry! Go ahead and eat.

145
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,642
What do you need? Fork?

146
00:10:08,642 --> 00:10:11,511
- Come on and eat.
- Hello?

147
00:10:11,511 --> 00:10:15,047
- Hello? Still nothing?
- Just go ahead and eat.

148
00:10:21,855 --> 00:10:23,490
<i>This is my world.</i>

149
00:10:23,490 --> 00:10:25,325
<i>Just like my family,</i>

150
00:10:25,325 --> 00:10:27,894
<i>the contents of our hearts are the same.</i>

151
00:10:27,894 --> 00:10:30,119
<i>Simple joys.</i>

152
00:10:30,119 --> 00:10:32,532
<i>We have no plans for world domination</i>

153
00:10:32,532 --> 00:10:35,735
<i>or expand our sphere of influence
in Eastern Europe.</i>

154
00:10:35,735 --> 00:10:39,172
<i>With us, even if Russia declares a war,</i>

155
00:10:39,172 --> 00:10:41,575
<i>we won't lose hope.</i>

156
00:10:41,575 --> 00:10:43,543
<i>We'll always fight.</i>

157
00:10:43,543 --> 00:10:44,511
Hello...

158
00:10:44,511 --> 00:10:46,613
- Here you go, Mr. Federico.
- Let me.

159
00:10:46,613 --> 00:10:47,848
Thank you.

160
00:10:47,848 --> 00:10:50,317
Hello? There...

161
00:10:50,317 --> 00:10:53,770
- Our dear friends...
- Our dear friends!

162
00:10:53,770 --> 00:10:57,140
Just a second.
There's something I want to tell you.

163
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,908
I just want to tell you

164
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:03,779
that the success of my daughter
is our success too.

165
00:11:06,983 --> 00:11:11,788
I hope she'll serve as
an inspiration to all of us,

166
00:11:11,788 --> 00:11:14,023
because there's nothing wrong
with dreaming, right?

167
00:11:14,023 --> 00:11:16,492
That's right.

168
00:11:16,492 --> 00:11:19,696
Even if we lose everything.

169
00:11:19,696 --> 00:11:25,335
Even if the trials of destiny
are thrown at us,

170
00:11:25,335 --> 00:11:30,467
they can never steal from us
our right to dream, right?

171
00:11:30,467 --> 00:11:32,708
Right?

172
00:11:34,794 --> 00:11:40,567
Let's dream of a beautiful tomorrow
for our loved ones.

173
00:11:40,567 --> 00:11:43,286
- Alright?
- Yes.

174
00:11:43,286 --> 00:11:45,388
That's why...

175
00:11:45,388 --> 00:11:47,023
This is for Florence.

176
00:11:47,023 --> 00:11:52,395
- For Florence.
- For Florence!

177
00:11:52,395 --> 00:11:54,225
And this is for all of us.

178
00:11:54,225 --> 00:11:58,013
- Yes, for all of us.
- Yes, for all of us!

179
00:11:58,013 --> 00:11:59,435
Federico?

180
00:11:59,435 --> 00:12:01,671
What happened?

181
00:12:01,671 --> 00:12:03,573
- Father?
- Move aside.

182
00:12:03,573 --> 00:12:05,141
- Move aside!
- Call an ambulance.

183
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:05,942
Help him!

184
00:12:05,942 --> 00:12:10,212
- Move aside.
- Move aside!

185
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:32,000
We still have money left.

186
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,104
I also called your grandfather.

187
00:12:35,104 --> 00:12:37,040
He said he'll help us out.

188
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:41,984
And even our relatives in Cebu,
they'll be giving money.

189
00:12:41,984 --> 00:12:46,082
The barangay captain
said she'll apply your father

190
00:12:46,082 --> 00:12:49,218
to the medical aid program of the mayor.

191
00:12:49,218 --> 00:12:53,496
But, Florence, I'm sorry.

192
00:12:53,496 --> 00:12:58,094
I have to ask you to take charge
of our food business.

193
00:12:58,094 --> 00:13:02,098
You take charge of delivering food
to the construction site.

194
00:13:02,098 --> 00:13:04,584
I don't want to lose that income.

195
00:13:04,584 --> 00:13:08,622
We can add that to
your father's after-surgery expenses

196
00:13:08,622 --> 00:13:14,343
and the money we need for medicines.

197
00:13:16,679 --> 00:13:19,849
We can handle this, my child.

198
00:13:19,849 --> 00:13:21,851
We can do this.

199
00:13:21,851 --> 00:13:24,553
We'll fight.

200
00:13:27,557 --> 00:13:30,026
We can do this, Mother.

201
00:13:30,026 --> 00:13:36,131
We will fight and we will win,
that's for sure.

202
00:13:51,013 --> 00:13:53,407
I'll go ahead.

203
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:59,621
Bye, Florence. Take care.

204
00:14:12,230 --> 00:14:14,799
Thank you, Mister, enjoy!

205
00:14:16,839 --> 00:14:18,674
Miss, would you like some cooked meals?
This is delicious.

206
00:14:18,674 --> 00:14:20,386
No, thank you.

207
00:14:20,386 --> 00:14:22,228
Okay.

208
00:14:25,214 --> 00:14:28,016
Let's hurry, we might get wet in the rain.

209
00:14:33,856 --> 00:14:37,160
Mister, this is for you. For you, Mister.

210
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:40,535
And this, Mister, this one is yours.

211
00:14:40,535 --> 00:14:43,299
Here, that's two orders, please.

212
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:46,702
But credit is not allowed at the moment.

213
00:14:46,702 --> 00:14:49,872
Father needs medicine and money
for his operation,

214
00:14:49,872 --> 00:14:53,413
so if it's okay, pay cash for now.

215
00:14:53,413 --> 00:14:55,311
Did you cook this, Florence?

216
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:56,445
Yes.

217
00:14:56,445 --> 00:14:58,147
Are you doubting the taste?

218
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:00,950
Don't worry, Mother taught me everything,

219
00:15:00,950 --> 00:15:03,733
so I'm sure it's as delicious.

220
00:15:03,733 --> 00:15:07,452
If you don't like it, I'll refund your money.

221
00:15:07,452 --> 00:15:09,702
Florence.

222
00:15:11,994 --> 00:15:13,835
What's this for?

223
00:15:14,764 --> 00:15:17,834
We all pitched in for your father.

224
00:15:17,834 --> 00:15:23,438
It's not much,
but we hope this can help Federico.

225
00:15:24,707 --> 00:15:27,510
Thank you. I won't say no to this.

226
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:30,913
This is a big help for us.

227
00:15:30,913 --> 00:15:34,750
By the way, here's your rice, Mister.

228
00:15:37,787 --> 00:15:40,323
Here you go, Mister. Thank you.

229
00:15:40,323 --> 00:15:42,642
Florence?

230
00:15:42,642 --> 00:15:44,810
Mr. Dencio.

231
00:15:46,429 --> 00:15:47,864
How are you?

232
00:15:47,864 --> 00:15:50,099
How's Federico?

233
00:15:50,099 --> 00:15:55,404
Well, he's fighting but don't worry,
he can handle that.

234
00:15:55,404 --> 00:15:58,267
You're the one doing that now?

235
00:15:58,267 --> 00:16:00,042
Yes.

236
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:04,013
I'm sorry, I don't have extra funds,

237
00:16:04,013 --> 00:16:06,115
but the reason
why I'm looking for you is that,

238
00:16:06,115 --> 00:16:09,218
I have a side hustle for you.

239
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:10,860
Side hustle?

240
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:13,890
All you have to do is cook delicious food.

241
00:16:13,890 --> 00:16:17,593
I know you're a very good cook,
so you can do that.

242
00:16:17,593 --> 00:16:19,328
Where will I cook?

243
00:16:19,328 --> 00:16:20,930
In the Ferell household.

244
00:16:20,930 --> 00:16:24,166
You just have to cook for the children.

245
00:16:26,002 --> 00:16:28,170
Do you know the Ferells?

246
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:31,874
They're one of the richest families
here in Levante.

247
00:16:31,874 --> 00:16:35,878
And I'm sure they pay a high salary,

248
00:16:35,878 --> 00:16:39,849
and that can be a big help
for your needs right now.

249
00:16:39,849 --> 00:16:41,617
That's true, Mr. Dencio.

250
00:16:41,617 --> 00:16:44,954
Is there anyone who doesn't know the Ferells?

251
00:16:44,954 --> 00:16:49,025
I think they are the richest family
here in Levante.

252
00:16:49,025 --> 00:16:52,395
And what I know,
their levels of riches are different.

253
00:16:52,395 --> 00:16:57,566
But is that all you know about the Ferells?

254
00:16:59,235 --> 00:17:01,570
Why, Mr. Dencio?

255
00:17:01,570 --> 00:17:05,763
Is there something I need to know
about the Ferells?

256
00:17:06,876 --> 00:17:09,111
Are they weird?

257
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:14,890
Do they eat the human heart
or internal organs?

258
00:17:14,890 --> 00:17:16,452
Not really.

259
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:22,627
They're just like us, they eat, sleep,
they get sad, and cry,

260
00:17:22,627 --> 00:17:23,859
but of course,

261
00:17:23,859 --> 00:17:29,699
the rich people think differently
compared to us, who are at the bottom.

262
00:17:29,699 --> 00:17:34,102
What do you mean, Mr. Dencio?

263
00:17:37,940 --> 00:17:39,742
Ferell...

264
00:17:39,742 --> 00:17:41,380
Let me search for it.

265
00:17:42,345 --> 00:17:44,347
Ferell...

266
00:17:44,347 --> 00:17:47,120
<i>This is the first time
I got insulted this way</i>

267
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:48,951
<i>by the grandchildren of Don Ferell.</i>

268
00:17:48,951 --> 00:17:51,153
<i>I will never forget this!</i>

269
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:52,788
<i>And I will tell everybody</i>

270
00:17:52,788 --> 00:17:55,992
<i>that the worst thing
that can happen to a chef</i>

271
00:17:55,992 --> 00:17:58,523
<i>is to cook for the Ferells.</i>

272
00:17:58,523 --> 00:18:03,966
<i>I will shout it out to ban them
by all the chefs.</i>

273
00:18:03,966 --> 00:18:05,835
<i>Ping, ping, ping!</i>

274
00:18:05,835 --> 00:18:07,470
What?

275
00:18:07,470 --> 00:18:10,106
Mr. Dencio, why should we continue?

276
00:18:10,106 --> 00:18:13,232
If the chefs couldn't stand a chance,
how can I?

277
00:18:14,178 --> 00:18:18,314
Just relax, that's why I'm here, right?

278
00:18:18,314 --> 00:18:20,416
So what if they don't get you?

279
00:18:20,416 --> 00:18:21,984
Will you lose anything?

280
00:18:21,984 --> 00:18:26,455
But if they choose you,
then the problem is solved.

281
00:18:26,455 --> 00:18:29,825
You know, there's a saying,

282
00:18:29,825 --> 00:18:32,928
you have everything to lose
and nothing to gain.

283
00:18:32,928 --> 00:18:34,764
It's the other way around, Mr. Dencio,

284
00:18:34,764 --> 00:18:38,167
you have nothing to lose
but everything to gain.

285
00:18:38,167 --> 00:18:39,235
See?

286
00:18:39,235 --> 00:18:41,470
I know that you know what is right,

287
00:18:41,470 --> 00:18:44,573
that's why, this is easy for you.

288
00:18:51,619 --> 00:18:53,249
You can do this, Florence.

289
00:18:53,249 --> 00:18:55,072
Just give it a try.

290
00:19:14,568 --> 00:19:17,562
Just go in. Wait for me.
I'll just park the car.

291
00:19:17,562 --> 00:19:20,164
- Okay, Mr. Dencio.
- All right.

292
00:20:07,723 --> 00:20:10,793
You should close your mouth.

293
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:13,674
Something bad might happen to you.

294
00:20:15,331 --> 00:20:16,332
I'm sorry.

295
00:20:16,332 --> 00:20:19,835
This mansion is beautiful and it's so big.

296
00:20:19,835 --> 00:20:22,775
Are you the one referred by Dencio?

297
00:20:23,672 --> 00:20:27,994
Yes. I'd like to apply as a cook
for the Ferells.

298
00:20:29,712 --> 00:20:31,510
Follow me.

299
00:20:32,414 --> 00:20:34,822
Walk this way.

300
00:20:43,993 --> 00:20:49,664
So this is the kitchen
and this will be your area.

301
00:20:54,737 --> 00:20:59,375
Now, I will be honest with you, Miss...

302
00:20:59,375 --> 00:21:02,077
Florence. It's Florence Dela Cruz.

303
00:21:02,077 --> 00:21:05,581
Alright, Ms. Florence Dela Cruz.

304
00:21:05,581 --> 00:21:11,837
I don't easily give a chance to anyone
to be a cook for the Ferells.

305
00:21:11,837 --> 00:21:15,578
I go through a long process of recruitment.

306
00:21:15,578 --> 00:21:20,863
Usually, highly recommended by people
in the culinary scenes.

307
00:21:20,863 --> 00:21:23,599
And at least, the very least,

308
00:21:23,599 --> 00:21:28,070
who has worked for a couple of years
in the top restaurants.

309
00:21:28,070 --> 00:21:31,243
It looks like no one stays long, right?

310
00:21:32,241 --> 00:21:33,268
I'm sorry.

311
00:21:33,268 --> 00:21:37,313
I saw the video of a chef
and if I'm not mistaken,

312
00:21:37,313 --> 00:21:40,849
they are cursing the Ferells.

313
00:21:40,849 --> 00:21:46,288
Well, at least you know why I'm so desperate.

314
00:21:46,288 --> 00:21:49,748
So desperate that I'm willing
to take a chance on you,

315
00:21:49,748 --> 00:21:51,816
who is a nobody.

316
00:21:52,628 --> 00:21:57,099
That's what we need in life,
a chance to make a difference.

317
00:21:57,099 --> 00:21:58,634
One chance to change the world

318
00:21:58,634 --> 00:22:01,203
and one chance to start a revolution.

319
00:22:01,203 --> 00:22:03,739
That's why, don't waste your one chance.

320
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:08,310
After all, it's not every day
that you're given a chance

321
00:22:08,310 --> 00:22:15,116
to cook for one of the most
influential families in Levante.

322
00:22:15,884 --> 00:22:19,455
Now, cook me your best recipe.

323
00:22:19,455 --> 00:22:24,460
Prove to me that you deserve
to be a cook in this mansion.

324
00:22:24,460 --> 00:22:29,265
Prove to me that you can cook
for the grandchildren of Don Ferell.

325
00:22:29,265 --> 00:22:33,705
Okay, I'll prove that I can cook
for the grandchildren of Don Ferell.

326
00:22:34,634 --> 00:22:35,771
What are you waiting for?

327
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:38,369
Do you have an apron?

328
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:03,690
I'll just get back to you.

329
00:24:23,178 --> 00:24:24,446
Just a moment.

330
00:24:24,446 --> 00:24:29,457
In a few minutes, you'll be able to
taste this delicious food that I cooked.

331
00:24:33,222 --> 00:24:35,827
Who are you?

332
00:24:40,529 --> 00:24:42,431
Don Ferell!

333
00:24:42,431 --> 00:24:44,566
Is there anything you need, Sir?

334
00:24:44,566 --> 00:24:48,337
By the way, she is Florence Dela Cruz.

335
00:24:48,337 --> 00:24:51,350
She's applying as a cook for the children.

336
00:24:54,743 --> 00:24:57,146
Isn't she too young?

337
00:24:57,146 --> 00:24:59,248
Who recommended her?

338
00:24:59,248 --> 00:25:03,072
Well, it's Dencio who recommended her.

339
00:25:03,072 --> 00:25:07,623
Since we still haven't found a chef,

340
00:25:07,623 --> 00:25:11,426
given the rumors about your grandchildren,

341
00:25:12,194 --> 00:25:14,163
I'll try her out.

342
00:25:14,163 --> 00:25:19,034
Maybe we can hire her
while we still can't find a cook

343
00:25:19,034 --> 00:25:22,403
with more credentials.

344
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:29,324
So, Florence Dela Cruz?

345
00:25:36,199 --> 00:25:40,308
I'm sorry if I surprised you
because when I saw you,

346
00:25:40,308 --> 00:25:41,957
I remembered someone.

347
00:25:42,858 --> 00:25:44,359
Never mind...

348
00:25:44,359 --> 00:25:45,627
That's okay.

349
00:25:45,627 --> 00:25:49,931
Even my father mistakes me
for Marian Rivera...

350
00:25:54,236 --> 00:25:57,671
and Bea Alonzo on this side.

351
00:26:03,579 --> 00:26:05,280
That's just a joke.

352
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:07,030
It's just a joke.

353
00:26:12,888 --> 00:26:16,792
That's also a joke.
You're a funny girl, Florence.

354
00:26:16,792 --> 00:26:19,137
You can call me Grandpa Garp.

355
00:26:19,137 --> 00:26:20,529
Because if you call me Don,

356
00:26:20,529 --> 00:26:24,520
people might think that we are characters
from an old drama series.

357
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:26,101
That's for sure!

358
00:26:26,101 --> 00:26:27,870
And if I'm not mistaken,

359
00:26:27,870 --> 00:26:30,506
Serafica here is making you audition.

360
00:26:30,506 --> 00:26:35,644
But with what I'm smelling,
it looks like your cooking skill passed.

361
00:26:35,644 --> 00:26:40,782
Serafica, can I be a judge of the new chef

362
00:26:40,782 --> 00:26:44,753
because I also want to taste
Ms. Dela Cruz's cooking?

363
00:26:44,753 --> 00:26:46,722
Of course, Don Ferell.

364
00:26:46,722 --> 00:26:48,374
No problem.

365
00:26:48,374 --> 00:26:52,082
And I think it would be best that you decide

366
00:26:52,082 --> 00:26:56,676
if she deserves to be hired as a cook
for the Ferell family.

367
00:27:08,544 --> 00:27:10,912
What is that?

368
00:27:15,817 --> 00:27:19,469
We call that Le Balbacua
de Familia Dela Cruz.

369
00:27:19,469 --> 00:27:20,956
That's my father's recipe

370
00:27:20,956 --> 00:27:24,773
which his father passed on to him
when he was still living in Tabunok.

371
00:27:24,773 --> 00:27:26,395
Oh, from the mountains?

372
00:27:26,395 --> 00:27:28,741
No, not from the mountains, it's Tabunok.

373
00:27:28,741 --> 00:27:32,067
It's one of the most beautiful places
to visit in Cebu.

374
00:27:32,067 --> 00:27:33,902
Have you been to Cebu?

375
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:36,905
If you have time I'll take you there and,
you know,

376
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:38,023
the beaches there are beautiful.

377
00:27:38,023 --> 00:27:40,890
It's so blue
and there are beautiful water resorts,

378
00:27:40,890 --> 00:27:44,246
there are slides, places like that,
Granda Garp.

379
00:27:44,246 --> 00:27:46,926
Oh, I mean, Don Ferell...

380
00:27:48,317 --> 00:27:53,787
Don Ferell, I think you should
taste what Ms. Florence cooked,

381
00:27:53,787 --> 00:27:59,261
so we'd know if she deserves
to be a cook in this household.

382
00:27:59,261 --> 00:28:01,925
What are we waiting for?

383
00:28:55,784 --> 00:28:57,764
Don Ferell?

384
00:29:00,088 --> 00:29:01,991
Are you all right?

385
00:29:02,905 --> 00:29:04,493
What have you done?

386
00:29:04,493 --> 00:29:06,774
What did you put in what you cooked?

387
00:29:06,774 --> 00:29:09,391
Huh? I didn't put anything there.

388
00:29:09,391 --> 00:29:10,966
Get out!

389
00:29:10,966 --> 00:29:12,334
I'm so sorry, Don Ferell.

390
00:29:12,334 --> 00:29:16,928
Maybe you're not used
to that kind of cooking.

391
00:29:16,928 --> 00:29:18,674
I knew it was a mistake.

392
00:29:18,674 --> 00:29:20,586
The moment she stepped into this house,

393
00:29:20,586 --> 00:29:23,612
I just knew there was a mistake because I...

394
00:29:23,612 --> 00:29:25,303
Actually...

395
00:29:26,582 --> 00:29:28,550
This thing is very good.

396
00:29:28,550 --> 00:29:31,311
It reminded me of the cooking of my wife.

397
00:29:34,122 --> 00:29:36,125
This is very good.

398
00:29:36,125 --> 00:29:40,796
It's very, very, very good.

399
00:29:40,796 --> 00:29:43,717
Are you sure, Don Ferell?

400
00:29:44,766 --> 00:29:46,571
Yes, I was just surprised.

401
00:29:46,571 --> 00:29:49,389
I wasn't expecting
that I'd be able to taste again

402
00:29:49,389 --> 00:29:53,280
a food cooked deliciously
like how my wife used to cook.

403
00:29:54,476 --> 00:29:57,319
So I guess you can say I'm impressed.

404
00:29:58,561 --> 00:30:02,684
You have a talent for cooking
and from what I can smell,

405
00:30:02,684 --> 00:30:04,850
you cook from the heart.

406
00:30:06,421 --> 00:30:08,703
So if you'll accept it,

407
00:30:08,703 --> 00:30:15,163
I want to say that you can now
be the cook for my family.

408
00:30:15,163 --> 00:30:16,175
What?

409
00:30:16,175 --> 00:30:19,166
It means you're hired, Miss.

410
00:30:19,987 --> 00:30:23,847
Really? Yeah! Thank you, Sir!

411
00:30:23,847 --> 00:30:26,141
Ms. Florence, please.

412
00:30:26,141 --> 00:30:28,610
Behave yourself.

413
00:30:28,610 --> 00:30:30,730
Don't worry, Don Ferell.

414
00:30:30,730 --> 00:30:32,664
I will orient Ms. Florence

415
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:36,184
on how to act properly
around you and the children.

416
00:30:36,184 --> 00:30:38,036
Just give me one week to train her.

417
00:30:38,036 --> 00:30:41,580
No need. She can start right away.

418
00:30:41,580 --> 00:30:44,602
And I think it's better if she meets the kids

419
00:30:44,602 --> 00:30:48,196
because after all,
she'll be cooking for them.

420
00:30:48,196 --> 00:30:50,365
Of course, Sir.

421
00:30:50,365 --> 00:30:52,663
I will call all of them.

422
00:30:53,508 --> 00:30:55,504
Tell them I'll meet them in the garden.

423
00:30:55,504 --> 00:30:58,163
Yes, Sir. Of course, right away.

424
00:30:58,163 --> 00:30:59,983
This is good.

425
00:30:59,983 --> 00:31:02,177
Thank you so much, Grandpa Garp.

426
00:31:02,177 --> 00:31:06,702
This is a big help to my family,
and I'm excited to meet the kids.

427
00:31:07,708 --> 00:31:10,351
I'm sure you'll like them, too.

428
00:31:15,780 --> 00:31:19,702
Tristan, your grandpa wants to see you.

429
00:31:24,053 --> 00:31:28,442
Aldus, your grandpa is waiting in the garden.

430
00:31:33,008 --> 00:31:37,697
Troy, your grandpa is in the garden,
waiting now.

431
00:31:43,819 --> 00:31:49,236
Owen, please, go to the garden now.

432
00:31:53,795 --> 00:31:55,764
Just be patient with Serafica.

433
00:31:55,764 --> 00:31:57,454
She can be very strict sometimes,

434
00:31:57,454 --> 00:32:00,168
but that's because she takes care of us well.

435
00:32:00,168 --> 00:32:03,586
But don't worry, she's nice.

436
00:32:03,586 --> 00:32:05,340
She's very loyal to our family.

437
00:32:05,340 --> 00:32:08,524
And she's been with us for so many years now,

438
00:32:08,524 --> 00:32:11,813
she will take care of all of your needs.

439
00:32:11,813 --> 00:32:15,729
She's kind, she let me audition
to be your cook.

440
00:32:15,729 --> 00:32:17,752
Well, your timing is perfect,

441
00:32:17,752 --> 00:32:21,823
we do need a cook for my grandchildren.

442
00:32:21,823 --> 00:32:24,492
You're so nice,
you love your grandchildren so much

443
00:32:24,492 --> 00:32:27,569
and you personally take care of them.

444
00:32:27,569 --> 00:32:31,233
Well, what's the sense of all the wealth
that I have

445
00:32:31,233 --> 00:32:35,737
if I won't be able to be with my family?

446
00:32:35,737 --> 00:32:38,573
One more thing, I'm already old.

447
00:32:38,573 --> 00:32:41,128
I won't stay long in this world, Florence.

448
00:32:41,128 --> 00:32:43,278
So might as well spend it with them.

449
00:32:43,278 --> 00:32:45,247
Don't talk that way.

450
00:32:45,247 --> 00:32:47,944
I'm sure you'll have more time to spend
with your grandchildren.

451
00:32:47,944 --> 00:32:49,081
And one more thing,

452
00:32:49,081 --> 00:32:52,003
I'm sure that all your grandchildren
are so cute.

453
00:32:52,003 --> 00:32:53,791
You be the judge.

454
00:32:54,890 --> 00:32:57,306
Oh, they're here.

455
00:33:42,637 --> 00:33:44,455
So you're here.

456
00:33:47,309 --> 00:33:49,161
Where is Nero?

457
00:33:50,463 --> 00:33:52,114
Right there, Grandpa.

458
00:34:26,593 --> 00:34:28,053
Nero!

459
00:34:30,077 --> 00:34:31,897
Good catch, Grandson.

460
00:34:32,821 --> 00:34:35,563
This is Florence.
Now that you've met Florence,

461
00:34:35,563 --> 00:34:37,258
I want all of you to be good to her

462
00:34:37,258 --> 00:34:41,313
because starting tomorrow,
she'll start to cook for us.

463
00:34:41,313 --> 00:34:43,665
Don't worry, Grandpa, we'll be good to her.

464
00:34:43,665 --> 00:34:46,234
Assuming she's a good cook.

465
00:34:46,234 --> 00:34:48,470
I'm sure of that.

466
00:34:48,470 --> 00:34:54,309
So, Florence, you are officially hired.

467
00:34:54,309 --> 00:34:55,610
Is that all, Grandpa?

468
00:34:55,610 --> 00:34:58,110
I still have to finish something.

469
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:08,390
Okay, you can go.

470
00:35:08,390 --> 00:35:10,892
- Bye, Florence.
- Bye.

471
00:35:10,892 --> 00:35:12,732
Good luck!

472
00:35:13,542 --> 00:35:15,193
Good luck.

473
00:35:17,162 --> 00:35:21,936
It looks like they're all nice,
so there won't be any problem.

474
00:35:27,842 --> 00:35:29,944
What are you saying?

475
00:35:29,944 --> 00:35:32,247
You'll be cooking in the Ferell's mansion?

476
00:35:32,247 --> 00:35:36,217
In the mansion of the richest family
in Levante?

477
00:35:37,285 --> 00:35:40,722
Do you think your father will agree to that?

478
00:35:40,722 --> 00:35:43,258
How did you get that job?

479
00:35:43,258 --> 00:35:45,093
Because of Mr. Dencio.

480
00:35:45,093 --> 00:35:47,529
He is Father's friend, who always hangs out

481
00:35:47,529 --> 00:35:49,297
at the construction site.

482
00:35:49,297 --> 00:35:53,268
It was him who told me
that the Ferells need a cook,

483
00:35:53,268 --> 00:35:55,937
and he recommended me.

484
00:35:55,937 --> 00:35:57,739
Of course, Mother, I gave it a try,

485
00:35:57,739 --> 00:36:00,408
since I've got nothing to lose, right?

486
00:36:00,408 --> 00:36:03,944
I wasn't expecting that I'd pass,

487
00:36:03,944 --> 00:36:06,915
because when I cooked
Father's special Balbacua,

488
00:36:06,915 --> 00:36:10,351
Don Ferell was so impressed.

489
00:36:10,351 --> 00:36:11,886
Even though, Florence.

490
00:36:11,886 --> 00:36:16,591
We can provide for your father's needs.

491
00:36:16,591 --> 00:36:21,763
No... Well, you still can't work
with that Ferell's.

492
00:36:21,763 --> 00:36:27,268
Mother, the salary is 40,000 pesos
every month.

493
00:36:27,268 --> 00:36:29,471
When will you start?

494
00:36:29,471 --> 00:36:31,973
Do you agree now?

495
00:36:31,973 --> 00:36:34,943
No. Still a no.

496
00:36:34,943 --> 00:36:38,993
Mother, think about it,
40,000 pesos every month.

497
00:36:38,993 --> 00:36:40,882
That's four-zero thousand.

498
00:36:40,882 --> 00:36:44,419
That would be a big help for us, Mother,
especially for Father.

499
00:36:44,419 --> 00:36:46,921
That's why, I don't want
to turn down the offer.

500
00:36:46,921 --> 00:36:50,391
It's not that, my child.

501
00:36:50,391 --> 00:36:52,727
What about your studies?

502
00:36:52,727 --> 00:36:58,600
You're supposed to start studying
at the university after the vacation.

503
00:36:58,600 --> 00:37:00,468
What about your dreams?

504
00:37:00,468 --> 00:37:03,771
I will just apply again next year.

505
00:37:03,771 --> 00:37:05,273
What?

506
00:37:05,273 --> 00:37:08,626
You'll give up the scholarship you received?

507
00:37:12,087 --> 00:37:13,727
Florence.

508
00:37:15,335 --> 00:37:20,682
I appreciate you helping out
with your Father's situation,

509
00:37:20,682 --> 00:37:23,892
but that's not your obligation.

510
00:37:23,892 --> 00:37:26,528
If there's someone who should find a way,

511
00:37:26,528 --> 00:37:28,796
that's us, your parents, who should do it.

512
00:37:28,796 --> 00:37:32,834
Yes, I understand that, Mother.

513
00:37:32,834 --> 00:37:35,203
But even if I'm a scholar in GU,

514
00:37:35,203 --> 00:37:38,506
I still need money
for my expenses while studying,

515
00:37:38,506 --> 00:37:42,277
like money for my allowance,
transportation fares, and for projects.

516
00:37:42,277 --> 00:37:44,171
That's expensive, Mother.

517
00:37:44,171 --> 00:37:46,214
And now that we are a bit tight on budget,

518
00:37:46,214 --> 00:37:49,784
do you think I'd like to add up
to our expenses?

519
00:37:49,784 --> 00:37:53,922
We're now finding ways to pay
for Father's treatment, right?

520
00:37:53,922 --> 00:37:56,424
I understand you, Florence.

521
00:37:56,424 --> 00:37:59,127
I appreciate your initiatives, but...

522
00:37:59,127 --> 00:38:02,664
Mother, believe me or not,

523
00:38:02,664 --> 00:38:04,566
I've thought about this carefully.

524
00:38:04,566 --> 00:38:06,234
I have made my decision.

525
00:38:06,234 --> 00:38:08,860
This is what I want to do.

526
00:38:11,439 --> 00:38:13,775
Mother, please don't get mad at me.

527
00:38:13,775 --> 00:38:16,477
It's not that I'm mad, my child.

528
00:38:16,477 --> 00:38:20,882
Maybe... Maybe I'm just annoyed

529
00:38:20,882 --> 00:38:24,652
because I'm feeling so helpless
in this situation.

530
00:38:24,652 --> 00:38:31,426
Imagine, it's us, your parents,
who are a hindrance to your dreams.

531
00:38:31,426 --> 00:38:34,829
Mother, my dream is to have
a happy and complete family.

532
00:38:34,829 --> 00:38:37,298
Because what would I do
with being successful in life

533
00:38:37,298 --> 00:38:40,435
if you and Father are not by my side, right?

534
00:38:40,435 --> 00:38:43,838
And, Mother, I can apply again next year.

535
00:38:43,838 --> 00:38:46,908
With my intelligence,
I'm sure someone will get me.

536
00:38:46,908 --> 00:38:48,943
Someone will accept me, Mother.

537
00:38:48,943 --> 00:38:50,812
If GU won't accept me,

538
00:38:50,812 --> 00:38:57,185
then I'll apply to UP, or DLSU, ADMU, or PIS.

539
00:38:57,185 --> 00:39:00,188
Mother, there are a lot of opportunities,

540
00:39:00,188 --> 00:39:06,224
but what's important now
is all hands on deck for Father.

541
00:39:10,732 --> 00:39:12,372
Okay...

542
00:39:13,901 --> 00:39:17,322
I will agree, but on one condition.

543
00:39:17,322 --> 00:39:21,115
The moment you have a hard time
in that mansion,

544
00:39:21,115 --> 00:39:24,612
you'll leave that place as soon as possible
and come home.

545
00:39:24,612 --> 00:39:26,481
- Understood?
- Yes, Mother.

546
00:39:26,481 --> 00:39:28,750
- Is that a promise?
- Yes, Mother, that's a promise.

547
00:39:28,750 --> 00:39:30,518
Cross my heart, even if lightning strikes me,

548
00:39:30,518 --> 00:39:33,221
or a crocodile eats me,
I promise that to you, Mother.

549
00:39:33,221 --> 00:39:35,723
- That's a promise?
- Promise!

550
00:39:35,723 --> 00:39:37,427
Very good.

551
00:39:40,895 --> 00:39:43,231
- Thank you, Mother.
- Take care of yourself there, my child.

552
00:39:43,231 --> 00:39:44,896
Take care.

553
00:39:52,540 --> 00:39:54,247
Is it just me?

554
00:39:57,412 --> 00:40:00,760
Or I find our new cook cute?

555
00:40:02,150 --> 00:40:05,019
There you go again
with your flirty ways, Aldus.

556
00:40:05,019 --> 00:40:08,713
Will you go after our new cook, Bro?

557
00:40:08,713 --> 00:40:11,359
Did I say I'll fall for her?

558
00:40:11,359 --> 00:40:15,029
All I'm saying is she's cute.

559
00:40:15,029 --> 00:40:17,865
Be careful, Aldus, that's where it starts.

560
00:40:17,865 --> 00:40:20,678
At first, you'll find someone cute,

561
00:40:20,678 --> 00:40:23,338
and after that,
you'll think of something else.

562
00:40:23,338 --> 00:40:27,175
And before you know it,
you're trapped already with her charms.

563
00:40:27,175 --> 00:40:29,096
How about you, Nero?

564
00:40:29,977 --> 00:40:34,682
It's like I'm watching
a romantic comedy earlier.

565
00:40:34,682 --> 00:40:38,519
The scene was in slow motion,
and as she was falling,

566
00:40:38,519 --> 00:40:41,302
Nero was there just in time.

567
00:40:41,302 --> 00:40:45,026
Not a second too early,
not a second too late,

568
00:40:45,026 --> 00:40:47,962
but just in time to catch her in his arms.

569
00:40:47,962 --> 00:40:50,565
You know if there's a title for this story,

570
00:40:50,565 --> 00:40:53,436
it would be "Caught in Nero's Arms".

571
00:40:54,946 --> 00:41:00,922
What, Nero, do you and Ms. Florence Dela Cruz
have a chance?

572
00:41:01,976 --> 00:41:03,745
Hey, Nero, are you still there?

573
00:41:03,745 --> 00:41:06,214
We're talking to you.

574
00:41:06,214 --> 00:41:09,720
Guys, stop bothering Nero,

575
00:41:09,720 --> 00:41:13,121
and please stop thinking
about our household cook.

576
00:41:13,121 --> 00:41:15,223
Aren't you ashamed?

577
00:41:15,223 --> 00:41:18,493
You're making our cook an object of desire.

578
00:41:18,493 --> 00:41:20,795
Just imagine the scandal
this will bring to our family,

579
00:41:20,795 --> 00:41:24,411
once they find out
we're taking advantage of our staff.

580
00:41:25,533 --> 00:41:27,755
Do you think Grandpa Garp will be happy?

581
00:41:29,337 --> 00:41:30,872
Owen is right.

582
00:41:30,872 --> 00:41:33,717
Stop picking on the new cook.

583
00:41:33,717 --> 00:41:38,513
But still begs the question,
will she last long?

584
00:41:38,513 --> 00:41:40,828
As for me, I can make her quit in one day.

585
00:41:40,828 --> 00:41:44,313
You know what's better, let's welcome her...

586
00:41:44,313 --> 00:41:45,906
The Ferell's style.

587
00:41:45,906 --> 00:41:47,355
I want that.

588
00:41:47,355 --> 00:41:50,725
- Give me some.
- That sounds fun.

589
00:41:50,725 --> 00:41:53,461
It's been a while
since we had a source of amusement.

590
00:41:53,461 --> 00:41:56,813
Remember Chef Boy Logro?

591
00:41:56,813 --> 00:41:59,600
Yes, we made a celebrity chef cry.

592
00:41:59,600 --> 00:42:01,772
How about you, Owen, are you in?

593
00:42:03,371 --> 00:42:05,072
This is ridiculous.

594
00:42:05,072 --> 00:42:08,443
Again, this is just a waste of my time.

595
00:42:08,443 --> 00:42:10,211
I'd rather write my songs.

596
00:42:10,211 --> 00:42:12,038
Then don't.

597
00:42:13,881 --> 00:42:16,284
How about you, Nero?

598
00:42:16,284 --> 00:42:18,152
Are you with us?

599
00:42:18,152 --> 00:42:19,654
You'll enjoy it here.

600
00:42:19,654 --> 00:42:22,482
We'll play a prank on the new cook.

601
00:42:27,451 --> 00:42:29,931
Weirdo.

602
00:42:29,931 --> 00:42:31,699
Stop picking on Nero.

603
00:42:31,699 --> 00:42:34,974
If he gets mad, you're bound to get hurt.

604
00:42:43,044 --> 00:42:46,814
Excuse me, Don Ferell,
I will retire for tonight.

605
00:42:46,814 --> 00:42:49,217
Do you still have something for me to do?

606
00:42:49,217 --> 00:42:51,185
Nothing, you can take the night off.

607
00:42:51,185 --> 00:42:53,909
Thank you, Sir. Good night.

608
00:42:59,159 --> 00:43:06,901
Is it just me, or does that girl, Florence,
look disturbingly familiar?

609
00:43:06,901 --> 00:43:08,344
Well...

610
00:43:08,344 --> 00:43:09,770
Remember there are rumors

611
00:43:09,770 --> 00:43:13,326
that Don Rogelio's granddaughter
is still alive?

612
00:43:15,309 --> 00:43:21,182
Could it be that she's a relative
of the Almeros?

613
00:43:21,182 --> 00:43:27,880
Sir, my ex-boyfriend told me once
that I look like Gretchen Barretto,

614
00:43:29,090 --> 00:43:33,052
but believe it or not, we're not related.

615
00:43:36,664 --> 00:43:39,400
Good one... Good one,
you made me laugh with that.

616
00:43:39,400 --> 00:43:42,069
You don't really think
that you look like Gretchen Barretto.

617
00:43:42,069 --> 00:43:44,839
I'm not joking, Sir.

618
00:43:44,839 --> 00:43:47,408
I honestly believe
that I have a big resemblance

619
00:43:47,408 --> 00:43:52,314
with Ms. Gretchen Barretto,
especially with my angle on the left.

620
00:43:55,283 --> 00:43:58,454
Actually, it's possible.

621
00:43:59,504 --> 00:44:02,709
There is. There's a resemblance.

622
00:44:02,709 --> 00:44:06,821
Well, Sir, if there's nothing else
you want me to do,

623
00:44:06,822 --> 00:44:08,885
then I bid you good night.

624
00:44:12,079 --> 00:44:15,281
Good night, Serafica...

625
00:44:18,018 --> 00:44:20,885
Gretchen Barretto?

626
00:44:40,167 --> 00:44:42,999
Relax, Florence.

627
00:44:43,000 --> 00:44:44,705
Maybe you're just worrying about your father,

628
00:44:44,705 --> 00:44:47,282
that's why, you're having nightmares.

629
00:45:11,512 --> 00:45:13,496
I'm sorry, my child...

630
00:45:14,813 --> 00:45:17,132
But don't worry.

631
00:45:17,133 --> 00:45:20,136
I won't ever stop...

632
00:45:20,136 --> 00:45:24,373
I won't stop until I find Celestina.

633
00:45:37,601 --> 00:45:39,570
- What's that?
- Sushi.

634
00:45:39,570 --> 00:45:41,367
I'm not going to eat that.

635
00:45:44,775 --> 00:45:48,312
Even a stray dog who hasn't eaten for months
won't eat that.

636
00:45:48,312 --> 00:45:50,399
And then you'll ask me to eat that?

637
00:45:50,400 --> 00:45:51,735
Are you crazy?

638
00:45:51,735 --> 00:45:56,433
I was very clear
that what I want is Guimaras mangoes.

639
00:46:01,309 --> 00:46:02,941
Are you okay?

640
00:46:05,355 --> 00:46:08,885
Now if you're really having a hard time
and you can't do it,

641
00:46:08,885 --> 00:46:11,839
I'll understand why you want to resign.

642
00:46:13,318 --> 00:46:18,253
Are you just a dream,
or it will be a reality?

643
00:46:20,130 --> 00:46:23,753
He's cute but is he a weirdo?

644
00:46:23,753 --> 00:46:27,170
Does he sound like a frog?

645
00:46:27,170 --> 00:46:30,511
Kokak, kokak, kokak.

646
00:46:40,931 --> 00:46:42,818
I don't have any desires for him.

647
00:46:42,819 --> 00:46:45,021
None, none, none.

648
00:46:45,021 --> 00:46:47,113
Is there really none?

649
00:46:48,424 --> 00:46:50,701
Have you been here for a long time?

650
00:46:50,701 --> 00:46:52,695
I think you're lost.

651
00:46:52,695 --> 00:46:54,564
Never, ever give up.

652
00:46:54,564 --> 00:46:56,745
You can do it.

653
00:47:00,603 --> 00:47:05,275
What if the person
whose heart you're knocking on

654
00:47:05,275 --> 00:47:10,634
won't let you in his life?

655
00:47:10,634 --> 00:47:13,449
If he really refused to let you in...

656
00:47:14,745 --> 00:47:16,186
I will keep on knocking...

657
00:47:16,186 --> 00:47:19,722
Knock, knock, knock, knock,
until he opens the door.

658
00:47:19,722 --> 00:47:22,634
If he refuses to open the door,
I will destroy the door.

659
00:47:22,634 --> 00:47:24,770
If I need to sneak into the house

660
00:47:24,770 --> 00:47:28,466
or go through the window
just to get in, I will do that.

661
00:47:28,467 --> 00:47:31,299
Or if I need to shout, I will shout,

662
00:47:31,300 --> 00:47:35,968
"Hey, let me in your heart!"

663
00:47:35,968 --> 00:47:38,847
I can feel
there's a lot of space in your heart,

664
00:47:38,847 --> 00:47:42,433
so let me in your heart
for the kind of beauty you're not expecting,

665
00:47:42,434 --> 00:47:44,199
like me.

666
00:47:44,200 --> 00:47:45,320
He will definitely let you in.

667
00:47:45,320 --> 00:47:46,434
He will let me in.

668
00:47:46,434 --> 00:47:50,067
Yes, let her into your heart!

669
00:47:52,520 --> 00:47:56,523
If you won't let her in,
I just don't know about you.
